#[section, $md:
    # Documentation

    Welcome to Moth. Start with the project tool, learn the core language in order and drop into the focused pages when you need a precise rule.

    The @./progress (progress matrix) tracks current implementation and backend coverage.

    ## Start here

    1. @./getting-started (Getting Started)
    2. @./language-overview (Language basics)
    3. @./bindings (Values and bindings)
    4. @./numbers (Numbers)
    5. @./casts (Casts)
    6. @./functions (Functions)
    7. @./branching (Branching)
    8. @./loops (Loops)
    9. @./structs (Structs)
    10. @./choices (Choices)
    11. @./errors (Errors, options and assertions)
    12. @./collections (Collections and maps)
    13. @./templates (Templates)
    14. @./constants (Constants and compile-time behaviour)
    15. @./aliases (Aliases)
    16. @./generics (Generics)
    17. @./traits (Traits)
    18. @./reactivity (Reactivity)
    19. @./memory (Memory and lifetimes)

    ## Projects and content

    - @./project-structure (Project structure)
